{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSAUBKbqZpZwhKCEvBn1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the two screens, sent through `Analytics.capture`. `flutter analyze` reports no issues, but I haven't run the app, so none of the events have been seen firing yet.\n\nEach event fires once per user action rather than on every change, following your colleague's note. That matters because you're on the PostHog free tier:\n- **Email and phone \"started\":** a flag means each sends one event, on the first character typed, not one per keystroke.\n- **Loan amount slider:** the event fires when the user lets go of the slider (`onChangeEnd`), not on every step of the drag.\n- **Offers scrolled:** the event fires when a scroll comes to a stop, with how far down the list it ended.\n- **Terms accepted:** fires only when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked.\n- **Continue tapped:** fires on the tap, before moving to the offers screen.\n\nEvent names and properties match the spec exactly, and the email and phone number are never sent.\n\nOne behaviour to know: the registration screen stays alive while the offers screen is open. So the email and phone \"started\" events fire once per registration flow, not again each time the user comes back from offers. ANSWER.md says how to change that if product wants it per visit.\n\nANSWER.md also says which parts of the note applied and which didn't. In short, the text-field, slider and scroll fixes applied. The focus-lost capture, tap/focus events and the PostHog debug-log check didn't: no event needs a field's final value, the spec has no tap events, and I didn't run the app. It also asks product whether repeated slider drags, re-ticking the terms box and repeated scrolls should count once or every time.\n\n`flutter analyze` rewrote `analysis_options.yaml` by itself, so I reverted that and deleted the generated `.dart_tool/